  "title": "Prisoner transfer?",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 3 of 10",
  "description": "Star Wars director George Lucas fell behind schedule in the first week of shooting (March 22, 1976) due to a rare Tunisian rainstorm, malfunctioning props, and electronic breakdowns. Other problems quickly arose. Anthony Daniels was literally stabbed by his own costume the first time he suited up as Protocol Droid C-3PO. Adding to Lucas' stress while shooting: most of the crew considered the project a \"children's film,\" rarely took their work seriously, and often found the entire affair unintentionally humorous. Many believed Lucas' fanciful tale would fail, but it would go on to become one of the greatest movie franchises of all time."
